# unit-watch-remove.vrs: unit-watch D24 (Session 1), the off-ground rule, two tries, the removal and the next wave in game.
# uw-wave at the mark uw-a (made by unit-watch.vrs; set again here): Chaos kills three of wave 1's four spiders with
# `.devkill` (max 3), so the one left is the only wave-1 spider and every strand finds it again; `.devstrand <guid> under
# 30` sinks it 30 m under the pond's ground (ground y about 0, so -30 stays above the watch's -100) while Chaos stands 150 m
# away. Within 25 s the log reads "stuck: … (off-ground)" then "recovered: … try 1/2"; the strand repeated after each
# recovery gives "try failed: … try 1/2 (still stuck)", "recovered: … try 2/2", "try failed: … try 2/2 (still stuck)" and
# "removed: … after 2 tries, no kill credit"; wave 1 is then cleared by the removal's staged despawn and "event uw-wave
# wave 2/2" follows within 10 s of it; `event info` shows "1 removed"; the admin stop's scoreboard holds Chaos's three
# `.devkill` kills only, one fewer than wave 1's count.
#
# Needs: what unit-watch.vrs needs (StallMinutes 10: a 1-minute backstop would mark the lone spider first); the strand
# radius 200 reaches the lone spider from the far spot. A native CHAR_Spider_Forest nearer the far spot than uw-a would be
# picked instead: check the first DEV STRAND line's x and z are within 20 m of uw-a.
# Run: --var AX=-1880 --var AZ=-1640 --var FX=-1730 --var FZ=-1640
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
chat .devtp ${AX} ${AZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to x=(?P<PX>-?[0-9.]+) y=-?[0-9.]+ z=(?P<PZ>-?[0-9.]+)
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .devmark uw-a
expect-log \[DEV MARK\] uw-a
chat .nyar event set uw-wave location here
expect-reply uw-wave location =
mark
chat .nyar event start uw-wave
expect-log event uw-wave started by manual timeout=20
expect-log event uw-wave wave 1/2 timeout=30
wait 8
chat .devkill -581295882 40 3
expect-log \[DEV KILL\] n=3
# Chaos 150 m away, then the lone spider sunk 30 m
chat .devtp ${FX} ${FZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .devstrand -581295882 under 30 200
expect-log \[DEV STRAND\] moved=1 how=under x=(?P<SX>-?[0-9.]+) y=(?P<SY>-?[0-9.]+) z=(?P<SZ>-?[0-9.]+)
expect-calc hypot(${SX} - ${PX}, ${SZ} - ${PZ}) <= 20 and ${SY} > -100
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave stuck: CHAR_Spider_Forest wave 1 \(off-ground\) timeout=25
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave recovered: CHAR_Spider_Forest try 1/2, [0-9]+ m \((group|player|anchor)\) timeout=10
chat .nyar event info uw-wave
expect-reply unit watch: 1 stuck now, 1 recovered, 0 removed
# the strand again: still stuck after the move is a failed try, then the second try
wait 3
chat .devstrand -581295882 under 30 200
expect-log \[DEV STRAND\] moved=1 how=under
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave try failed: CHAR_Spider_Forest try 1/2 \(still stuck\) timeout=25
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave recovered: CHAR_Spider_Forest try 2/2, [0-9]+ m \((group|player|anchor)\) timeout=10
wait 3
chat .devstrand -581295882 under 30 200
expect-log \[DEV STRAND\] moved=1 how=under
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave try failed: CHAR_Spider_Forest try 2/2 \(still stuck\) timeout=25
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave removed: CHAR_Spider_Forest wave 1 after 2 tries, no kill credit timeout=10
# the removal cleared wave 1: the next wave comes
expect-log event uw-wave wave 1 cleared timeout=10
expect-log event uw-wave wave 2/2 timeout=10
chat .nyar event info uw-wave
expect-reply unit watch: 0 stuck now, 2 recovered, 1 removed
shot full uw-removed-info
# the scoreboard: Chaos's three kills, no credit for the removal
chat .nyar event stop uw-wave
expect-log event uw-wave stopped
expect-log event uw-wave scoreboard: 1 players, 3 kills, 0 deaths
expect-chat scoreboard: 1. Chaos 3 kills timeout=20
shot full uw-scoreboard
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
console TPHome
wait 3
